1
00:02:09,996 --> 00:02:39,976
We'll be right back.

2
00:02:39,996 --> 00:03:09,976
We'll be right back.

3
00:03:09,996 --> 00:03:39,976
We'll be right back.

4
00:03:39,976 --> 00:03:41,976
We'll be right back.

5
00:03:41,976 --> 00:03:43,976
Say you want to live.

6
00:03:43,976 --> 00:03:47,976
We are your friends!

7
00:03:47,976 --> 00:03:49,976
Shoot him down!

8
00:03:49,976 --> 00:03:51,976
Come on!

9
00:03:51,976 --> 00:03:52,976
Go!

10
00:03:52,976 --> 00:03:53,976
Get moving!

11
00:03:53,976 --> 00:03:55,976
Don't you remember what your mom told you?

12
00:03:55,976 --> 00:03:57,976
You must live, Robin!

13
00:03:57,976 --> 00:04:01,976
Attention evacuees!

14
00:04:01,976 --> 00:04:03,976
The ship is leaving!

15
00:04:03,976 --> 00:04:05,976
Wait! Someone's coming!

16
00:04:05,976 --> 00:04:07,976
It's her!

17
00:04:07,976 --> 00:04:09,976
Isn't that the monster girl?

18
00:04:09,976 --> 00:04:10,976
The monster girl?

19
00:04:10,976 --> 00:04:11,976
Yeah, it is!

20
00:04:11,976 --> 00:04:12,976
Go away!

21
00:04:12,976 --> 00:04:13,976
You're creepy!

22
00:04:13,976 --> 00:04:14,976
Hey!

23
00:04:14,976 --> 00:04:15,976
Now's not the time for that!

24
00:04:15,976 --> 00:04:16,976
Now wait!

25
00:04:16,976 --> 00:04:19,976
That kid's mother, Ovia, was in the newspaper just the other day.

26
00:04:19,976 --> 00:04:21,976
That means she's the daughter of a criminal!

27
00:04:21,976 --> 00:04:22,976
You're right!

28
00:04:22,976 --> 00:04:24,976
If we let her on the ship, it might cause us trouble!

29
00:04:24,976 --> 00:04:25,976
Just leave her!

30
00:04:25,976 --> 00:04:26,976
Don't be ridiculous!

31
00:04:26,976 --> 00:04:27,976
She's just a child!

32
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:28,976
Hurry up and help her!

33
00:04:28,976 --> 00:04:29,976
Everyone stop!

34
00:04:29,976 --> 00:04:31,976
Don't let that brat on board!

35
00:04:31,976 --> 00:04:32,976
Huh?

36
00:04:32,976 --> 00:04:35,976
She may be a child, but she's still an archaeologist!

37
00:04:35,976 --> 00:04:38,976
That means she's a criminal like the rest of them!

38
00:04:38,976 --> 00:04:39,976
A little girl like that?

39
00:04:39,976 --> 00:04:41,976
If you say so, Chief!

40
00:04:41,976 --> 00:04:42,976
See?

41
00:04:42,976 --> 00:04:43,976
I told you!

42
00:04:43,976 --> 00:04:44,976
Good thing we didn't let her on!

43
00:04:44,976 --> 00:04:45,976
Robin!

44
00:04:46,976 --> 00:04:47,976
Must be CP9!

45
00:04:47,976 --> 00:04:48,976
Damn!

46
00:04:48,976 --> 00:04:49,976
I'll show them!

47
00:04:49,976 --> 00:04:50,976
Chief!

48
00:04:50,976 --> 00:04:52,976
Vice Admiral Saul is coming this way!

49
00:04:52,976 --> 00:04:53,976
Is that so?

50
00:04:53,976 --> 00:04:56,976
Then there was no need to question Ovia about him after all!

51
00:04:56,976 --> 00:04:57,976
Fire!

52
00:04:57,976 --> 00:04:58,976
Now!

53
00:04:58,976 --> 00:04:59,976
Shoot him down!

54
00:04:59,976 --> 00:05:01,976
Ice block!

55
00:05:04,976 --> 00:05:05,976
Partisan!

56
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:10,976
No!

57
00:05:18,976 --> 00:05:20,976
It's Kuzan!

58
00:05:20,976 --> 00:05:21,976
You!

59
00:05:21,976 --> 00:05:22,976
My, my, my!

60
00:05:22,976 --> 00:05:24,976
This just won't do!

61
00:05:24,976 --> 00:05:28,976
If we let a former Marine stop the Buster Call, we'd look like damn fools!

62
00:05:28,976 --> 00:05:34,976
Shkuzan, wake up! You can't tell me this nonsense is justice!

63
00:05:34,976 --> 00:05:40,976
Pull back now! You know this ain't right! They're just making an example out of Ohara!

64
00:05:40,976 --> 00:05:43,976
Come on, please! You're better than this!

65
00:05:43,976 --> 00:05:50,976
If it's for the good of the world, it has to be done. You can't deny that those scholars are breaking the law, can you?

66
00:05:50,976 --> 00:05:57,976
I won't criticize your sense of justice. There are as many rights and wrongs as there are viewpoints in the world.

67
00:05:57,976 --> 00:06:04,976
However, if you insist on getting in our way, I can't sit back and do nothing.

68
00:06:12,976 --> 00:06:15,976
The evacuation ship was blown up! What happened?

69
00:06:15,976 --> 00:06:18,976
Looks like cannon fire from one of our ships!

70
00:06:18,976 --> 00:06:21,976
It was Vice Admiral Sakazuki!

71
00:06:21,976 --> 00:06:25,976
That idiot. If we're doing this, we have to be thorough.

72
00:06:25,976 --> 00:06:33,976
If even one of those scholars had managed to sneak on board that ship, then all the sacrifices we made today would be in vain.

73
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:37,976
However small, we cannot allow any evil to thrive.

74
00:06:37,976 --> 00:06:42,976
Is this what you call justice? Can you take pride in something like this?

75
00:06:42,976 --> 00:06:45,976
We went too far! I would never do something like that!

76
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:47,976
We gotta run, Robin!

77
00:06:47,976 --> 00:06:49,976
This fellow's way too strong for me to fight!

78
00:06:49,976 --> 00:06:53,976
Sol is escaping! He's taking one of the scholars with him!

79
00:06:53,976 --> 00:06:58,976
Ice time, capsule!

80
00:06:58,976 --> 00:07:04,976
Oh no! Sol, are you okay?

81
00:07:04,976 --> 00:07:13,976
Robin, you gotta get out of here!

82
00:07:13,976 --> 00:07:21,976
Don't look back! Just go! If you stay on this island, you'll die! Take my raft and go out to sea!

83
00:07:21,976 --> 00:07:22,976
But what about you?

84
00:07:22,976 --> 00:07:27,976
He's got me, little lady. I'm afraid this is the end. Hurry!

85
00:07:27,976 --> 00:07:30,976
No! Everybody I care about is here!

86
00:07:30,976 --> 00:07:38,976
Now you listen to me. You may be lonely at first, but one day you'll find true friends!

87
00:07:38,976 --> 00:07:42,976
True friends?

88
00:07:42,976 --> 00:07:43,976
True friends?

89
00:07:43,976 --> 00:07:47,976
Yeah. The sea's a vast place, so I guarantee!

90
00:07:47,976 --> 00:07:52,976
Some day you'll find friends who won't ever leave you!

91
00:07:52,976 --> 00:07:57,976
No matter who you are, ain't no one born into this world to be alone!

92
00:08:00,976 --> 00:08:03,976
It's time to go, Robin! This is goodbye!

93
00:08:03,976 --> 00:08:06,976
When things are bad, do like I taught you!

94
00:08:06,976 --> 00:08:08,976
You remember the laugh, don't you?

95
00:08:08,976 --> 00:08:09,976
Look out! He's behind you!

96
00:08:09,976 --> 00:08:11,976
Daddy, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh.

97
00:08:12,976 --> 00:08:13,976
Now, ice time.

98
00:08:16,976 --> 00:08:17,976
Oh no!

99
00:08:17,976 --> 00:08:20,976
Daddy, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh, sh.

100
00:08:20,976 --> 00:08:23,976
Your friends are out there at sea waiting for you, Robin.

101
00:08:23,976 --> 00:08:26,976
All you gotta do is find them.

102
00:08:29,976 --> 00:08:33,976
Share your life with them and never let them go.

103
00:08:33,976 --> 00:08:35,976
Ahh, Ahh, Ahh, Ahh!

104
00:08:36,976 --> 00:08:38,976
Yes!

105
00:08:45,976 --> 00:08:48,476
This is it. We're done for.

106
00:08:48,476 --> 00:08:52,476
So this is the history that mankind has chosen.

107
00:08:52,476 --> 00:08:56,476
Shall we ever learn the error of our ways?

108
00:08:56,476 --> 00:08:58,976
Forgive me, Robin.

109
00:09:00,476 --> 00:09:04,476
I couldn't even leave you with any parting words,

110
00:09:04,476 --> 00:09:08,476
neither is a skull or a mother.

111
00:09:08,476 --> 00:09:11,476
A tree of knowledge! It's falling!

112
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:24,476
The concept of absolute justice can sometimes drive a man to madness.

113
00:09:24,476 --> 00:09:26,476
I've decided to let you escape.

114
00:09:26,476 --> 00:09:31,476
I'm curious to see what kind of flower will sprout from the seed that's all protected.

115
00:09:31,476 --> 00:09:34,476
You can bear a grudge against whoever you like for this,

116
00:09:34,476 --> 00:09:36,476
but at least you're still alive.

117
00:09:36,476 --> 00:09:40,476
However, I do suggest you keep a low profile.

118
00:09:40,476 --> 00:09:44,476
I've drawn a path for you on the sea with my ice.

119
00:09:44,476 --> 00:09:48,476
If you take the boat and go straight ahead, you'll reach land eventually.

120
00:09:48,476 --> 00:09:51,476
Oh, one last thing.

121
00:09:51,476 --> 00:09:54,476
I'm not your ally.

122
00:09:54,476 --> 00:09:59,476
If you do cause any trouble, I'll be the first person to come after you.

123
00:09:59,476 --> 00:10:02,476
My mom's here! Can you help her?

124
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:04,476
No one will be saved.

125
00:10:04,476 --> 00:10:08,476
If that pain is too great for you to bear, then you may join them.

126
00:10:08,476 --> 00:10:11,476
This library is the best in the world.

127
00:10:11,476 --> 00:10:14,476
You like to read books?

128
00:10:14,476 --> 00:10:16,476
Today is Robin's birthday!

129
00:10:16,476 --> 00:10:19,476
Happy birthday from us at the library!

130
00:10:19,476 --> 00:10:21,476
Your mama's a wonderful woman.

131
00:10:21,476 --> 00:10:23,476
Our heart is a wonderful place.

132
00:10:23,476 --> 00:10:28,476
And as surely as we believe in the past, we believe in the future that you will inherit.

133
00:10:28,476 --> 00:10:31,476
When you're feeling down, just laugh.

134
00:10:31,476 --> 00:10:34,476
There ain't nothing a good laugh can't fix.

135
00:10:34,476 --> 00:10:36,476
It seems awfully silly to laugh when you're sad.

136
00:10:36,476 --> 00:10:38,976
Don't knock it till you try it!

137
00:10:58,476 --> 00:10:59,516
fifteen fifteen...

138
00:11:28,476 --> 00:11:38,036
The sea's a vast place, so I guarantee someday you'll find friends who won't ever leave you.

139
00:11:58,476 --> 00:12:06,556
Survivors? No, I don't think so.

140
00:12:07,916 --> 00:12:11,256
Hey! Huh? Come here, look at the lake!

141
00:12:12,316 --> 00:12:14,196
What? That's insane!

142
00:12:19,996 --> 00:12:21,916
How did all those books get here?

143
00:12:22,636 --> 00:12:24,036
It can't be a coincidence.

144
00:12:25,116 --> 00:12:26,216
Yeah, this is her!

145
00:12:27,136 --> 00:12:30,796
That's definitely the girl. Where did you find her? Is she captured?

146
00:12:31,176 --> 00:12:34,136
No. We were told to keep watch for a suspicious girl.

147
00:12:34,356 --> 00:12:36,956
We eventually found her on a passenger ship northeast of Ohara.

148
00:12:37,376 --> 00:12:41,216
Unfortunately, she knew what we were after, so she slipped away before we could catch her.

149
00:12:42,056 --> 00:12:43,696
She's got the devil's luck.

150
00:12:44,336 --> 00:12:46,636
Back then, I'm sure I saw her leaving Ohara.

151
00:12:47,116 --> 00:12:51,576
The island was burning to ash, but she somehow made it out alone on a little rowboat.

152
00:12:51,576 --> 00:12:57,616
Of course, I tried to chase her, but all of a sudden, the helm of our boat got stuck like it was frozen in ice.

153
00:12:57,996 --> 00:13:01,356
Either way, Saul probably helped her escape before he died.

154
00:13:02,036 --> 00:13:06,876
A scholar with the ability to read the poneglyphs is dangerous no matter how young she may be.

155
00:13:06,876 --> 00:13:10,896
I don't care what methods you use.

156
00:13:11,056 --> 00:13:15,296
If we don't capture her immediately, then this entire mission will have been for nothing.

157
00:13:19,456 --> 00:13:21,156
79 million berries?

158
00:13:21,536 --> 00:13:24,576
Why does an eight-year-old child have such a high bounty?

159
00:13:25,216 --> 00:13:27,056
They said she's one of the devils of Ohara.

160
00:13:27,536 --> 00:13:29,616
You know, those scholars who are plotting to end the world?

161
00:13:30,236 --> 00:13:30,676
Really?

162
00:13:30,676 --> 00:13:33,916
I heard she's saying six marine battleships, too.

163
00:13:34,116 --> 00:13:36,016
She must have some kind of weird power.

164
00:13:36,496 --> 00:13:38,436
Well, that explains the bounty.

165
00:13:39,156 --> 00:13:41,896
The government forces and navy leaders are searching for her, too.

166
00:13:42,596 --> 00:13:46,056
She probably wants to carry out the same plan as the scholars that were executed.

167
00:13:46,776 --> 00:13:49,716
If she's out for revenge, then no one is safe.

168
00:13:50,376 --> 00:13:52,636
We can't let a child of the devil run wild.

169
00:13:53,596 --> 00:13:55,136
Such a kind girl.

170
00:13:55,396 --> 00:13:56,816
Thank you for helping me out.

171
00:13:56,816 --> 00:13:57,456
Sure.

172
00:13:57,776 --> 00:13:59,736
I'm grateful for any work I can get.

173
00:14:00,156 --> 00:14:04,576
By the way, before we have our dinner, some men are here to see you.

174
00:14:06,016 --> 00:14:07,356
Don't let her get away!

175
00:14:07,456 --> 00:14:08,756
No, give me my money!

176
00:14:09,036 --> 00:14:11,176
I told you where she was hiding, didn't I?

177
00:14:11,336 --> 00:14:14,556
She may be small, but she still works hard.

178
00:14:16,636 --> 00:14:17,456
What's wrong?

179
00:14:17,696 --> 00:14:18,676
Having trouble sleeping?

180
00:14:19,016 --> 00:14:21,096
We have to get up early tomorrow to go to work.

181
00:14:21,336 --> 00:14:22,176
So rest well.

182
00:14:22,596 --> 00:14:22,896
Okay.

183
00:14:22,896 --> 00:14:27,276
She's sweet, but if we keep her around, we could get in serious trouble.

184
00:14:28,096 --> 00:14:30,036
Besides, just look at this bounty.

185
00:14:31,236 --> 00:14:31,716
Honey!

186
00:14:32,016 --> 00:14:33,196
She isn't in her room!

187
00:14:33,716 --> 00:14:34,276
Damn it!

188
00:14:34,596 --> 00:14:36,196
She must have overheard us talking.

189
00:14:41,536 --> 00:14:42,936
Damn it, she, she, she, she.

190
00:14:43,196 --> 00:14:44,036
You're hungry?

191
00:14:44,596 --> 00:14:45,056
Sorry.

192
00:14:45,456 --> 00:14:45,936
Me, too.

193
00:14:46,656 --> 00:14:47,576
Damn it, she, she, she.

194
00:14:48,136 --> 00:14:49,356
Damn it, she, she, she.

195
00:14:49,356 --> 00:14:54,476
Seems we're both wanted by the law, Robin.

196
00:14:55,416 --> 00:14:57,956
I know all about you.

197
00:14:58,316 --> 00:15:00,876
Work for me and I'll make sure you never go hungry.

198
00:15:03,576 --> 00:15:04,176
Captain!

199
00:15:04,476 --> 00:15:05,756
The Marines are after us!

200
00:15:05,996 --> 00:15:07,136
Where did Robin go?

201
00:15:07,256 --> 00:15:08,536
Hand her over, damn it!

202
00:15:08,796 --> 00:15:09,476
Hooray!

203
00:15:09,936 --> 00:15:11,436
That girl is bad luck!

204
00:15:11,436 --> 00:15:16,916
A devil like you shouldn't even exist!

205
00:15:17,916 --> 00:15:18,396
What?

206
00:15:18,616 --> 00:15:19,776
Nico Robin's here?

207
00:15:19,956 --> 00:15:20,476
Where at?

208
00:15:20,596 --> 00:15:21,556
Hunt her down!

209
00:15:21,696 --> 00:15:22,876
Turn her into the government!

210
00:15:27,396 --> 00:15:28,836
I can't believe it.

211
00:15:29,416 --> 00:15:30,396
A poneglyph.

212
00:15:30,396 --> 00:15:32,116
Stay away!

213
00:15:32,356 --> 00:15:34,476
I have nothing to sell to the likes of you!

214
00:15:35,136 --> 00:15:36,016
Look, I'm 16.

215
00:15:36,496 --> 00:15:37,256
I'll do anything.

216
00:15:37,776 --> 00:15:39,556
Please, just allow me to join your group.

217
00:15:39,936 --> 00:15:41,856
You betrayed me, you damn witch!

218
00:15:43,756 --> 00:15:44,856
Nico Robin.

219
00:15:45,616 --> 00:15:47,376
I'd like you to assist me.

220
00:15:49,296 --> 00:15:52,556
I've been told you can read Poneglyphs.

221
00:15:52,556 --> 00:16:00,716
If you trigger a buster call, everything will be destroyed.

222
00:16:01,516 --> 00:16:03,876
That includes all of Eni's lobby.

223
00:16:07,016 --> 00:16:09,916
And most likely, you as well.

224
00:16:10,556 --> 00:16:11,196
Nonsense!

225
00:16:11,716 --> 00:16:12,676
What are you saying?

226
00:16:13,336 --> 00:16:15,316
They wouldn't kill a VIP like me!

227
00:16:15,656 --> 00:16:17,456
I'm not falling for your bluff!

228
00:16:17,996 --> 00:16:21,636
20 years ago, everything was taken from me.

229
00:16:21,636 --> 00:16:24,136
And many innocent lives were lost.

230
00:16:24,716 --> 00:16:26,596
With one push of a button,

231
00:16:27,176 --> 00:16:28,836
they summoned a terrible demon.

232
00:16:29,856 --> 00:16:31,656
Now it rears its head again,

233
00:16:32,136 --> 00:16:35,456
aiming its sights on the friends I've searched so hard to find.

234
00:16:36,056 --> 00:16:38,196
The more that I wish for us to be together,

235
00:16:38,756 --> 00:16:42,416
the more my ugly fate bears its fangs at you.

236
00:16:43,436 --> 00:16:45,996
Even now, no matter how far we sail,

237
00:16:46,336 --> 00:16:48,436
there's an enemy that haunts me at every turn.

238
00:16:49,296 --> 00:16:51,256
Because I'm facing the world,

239
00:16:51,636 --> 00:16:52,996
and all of its darkness.

240
00:16:53,996 --> 00:16:55,176
First it was Aokiji,

241
00:16:55,656 --> 00:16:57,016
and now CP9.

242
00:16:57,396 --> 00:16:59,996
I've dragged you into my troubles twice already!

243
00:17:01,036 --> 00:17:03,316
If it goes on and on like this,

244
00:17:03,836 --> 00:17:05,696
no matter how kind you may be,

245
00:17:06,396 --> 00:17:08,876
someday you'll see me as a burden!

246
00:17:09,436 --> 00:17:12,296
Someday you'll be forced to betray me and throw me away!

247
00:17:12,636 --> 00:17:14,396
That's what I'm most afraid of!

248
00:17:14,396 --> 00:17:15,216
Understand?

249
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,616
That's why I didn't want you to rescue me!

250
00:17:17,816 --> 00:17:19,856
If that's the only future I have,

251
00:17:19,976 --> 00:17:22,416
I'd rather die to save me the pain!

252
00:17:27,196 --> 00:17:27,756
Robin...

253
00:17:27,756 --> 00:17:29,376
I never knew.

254
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:31,776
Robin...

255
00:17:31,776 --> 00:17:34,136
I see.

256
00:17:34,456 --> 00:17:35,376
So that's it.

257
00:17:36,116 --> 00:17:37,216
